Comment (cmd/reconciler.go:340):
Blocking (behaviour regression, "no breaking changes"): on `main`, a plugin or policy download failure at startup went through `Run` and called `sendAgentRunEvidenceOnStartupFailure` (agent evidence enabled with `emit_on_run_completion`, which is the default) before exiting 1. That is how CCF learns that an agent failed to start. Now the file-only rung's `Prefetch` failure returns here, `agentRunner` exits 1, and `Run` never executes, so that evidence is never sent. `markPluginsWithSourceFailed` and `markPluginsWithPolicyFailed` never run either, so even a later send would lack the failure details.

Suggested fix: when the last (file-only) rung fails with `download-failed`, fall through to `Run` with the file-only runtime, as `main` did, so the existing failure-evidence path fires. Or explicitly `UpdateConfig` and send the startup-failure evidence before returning. The exit code stays 1. Please add a test that asserts the startup-failure evidence is sent.
Replies:
**lisa implementation guidance:** Fix: Prefetch returns a typed download error (plugin vs policy source). prepare attaches the built runtime to the download-failed applyError; startup, when the file-only rung fails with download-failed, calls an onStartupFailure hook (wired to AgentRunner) that UpdateConfig()s the runtime, marks the plugins with the failed source/policy (markPluginsWith*Failed) and sends sendAgentRunEvidenceOnStartupFailure before returning (exit 1 unchanged). Test asserts the evidence is sent with the failure.

