Comment (cmd/reconciler.go:392):
Non-blocking: rejected-revision memory (and `inFailedBackoff`) match on ETag alone. If a response ever arrives without an `ETag` header (a stripping proxy, or an API bug), every revision has `ETag == ""`. One rejection then blocks all later revisions until the base changes. I confirmed this in a probe: an unsafe rev 1, then a safe rev 2, both with an empty ETag → rev 2 is never applied. `sameOverlay` already falls back to revision plus bytes when the ETag is empty. Suggest the same fallback here, i.e. key on `(revision, sha256(overlay))` when `ETag == ""`.
Replies:
**lisa implementation guidance:** Fix: key the rejected memory and failed backoff on overlayKey(rec): the ETag when set, else revision + sha256(overlay). RejectedRecord gains overlay_sha256 (omitempty, cache stays compatible). Test: empty ETag, unsafe rev 1 then safe rev 2 -> rev 2 applies.

