Comment (internal/inlinepolicy/materialize.go:251):
Non-blocking: `WalkDir` doesn't follow a symlinked **root**. If a local `extends` (or the resolved policy root) is itself a symlink, e.g. `/etc/ccf/policies` → a versioned dir, or a k8s ConfigMap mount whose files are `..data/*` links, the vendor tree comes back empty or with odd `..2024_…/` paths. It is reported only as a warning, and the materialized bundle silently loses the vendor policies. Suggest `filepath.EvalSymlinks(dir)` on the root before walking, and possibly following in-tree symlinks whose target stays under the resolved root. Keep skipping the ones that escape it.
Replies:
**lisa implementation guidance:** Fix (cheap part): readTree resolves the root with filepath.EvalSymlinks before walking; Materialize returns ErrResolve (download-failed, retried with backoff) when an extends tree has no .rego file. In-tree symlinks stay skipped (warning). Tests: symlinked extends root, empty extends tree.

