Comment (cmd/inline.go:187):
Non-blocking: GC runs only at startup, and `Materialize` writes the directory before `Check`, so rejected content also lands on disk. A long-running daemon accumulates one directory per distinct revision or bundle content (up to 1 MiB each) until it restarts. The design allows "GC on start", but a GC after each successful swap, keeping the active and pending dirs plus the newest N, would bound it cheaply.
Replies:
**lisa implementation guidance:** Fix: run inline GC after every successful swap, keeping the dirs of the running and the pending candidate plus the newest inlineGCKeepPerBundle per bundle (shared helper with the startup GC).

